<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Donyö Dorje</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1512">1512</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Donyo Dorje</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Donyö Dorje was the most powerful ruler of the Rinpungpa dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsang">Tsang</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>. Around 1498 his forces took control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a> region, and as patron of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karma-kagyu">Karma Kagyu</a> school he barred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelug">Gelug</a> monks from Lhasa's Great Prayer Festival until 1517. His reign marked the height of Rinpungpa dominance over the Phagmodrupa rulers.</p></div>
